c592d7"} {"question" "q-130888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-1-4\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ -3\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/state.json" "file_sha256" "a9302120e50a88bb29d91cba43d547f5184d2c95789086b343ed6ba943c592d7"} {"question" "q-130888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4b86640334b0f49f7977fb59639aabb6d7aff9789dae17642a4e607e693d252"} {"question" "q-130888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/st