ld" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+bc?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/state.json" "file_sha256" "a9302120e50a88bb29d91cba43d547f5184d2c95789086b343ed6ba943c592d7"} {"question" "q-38388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=2,b=5,c=4$ and $d=-2$, which implies that \n\n$$\nad+bc=2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 4=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/state.json" "file_sha256" "a9302120e50a88bb29d91cba43d547f5184d2c95789086b343ed6ba943c592d7"} {"question" "q-38388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4b86640334b0f49f7977fb59639aabb6d7aff9789dae17642a4e607e693d252"} {"question" "q-38388" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/state.json" "file_sha256" "a9302120e50a88bb29d91cba43d547f5184d2c95789086b343ed6ba